@cc [author:spolu,label:evaluation] matched-arm-parity
For each scored task and attempt, `control` and `code-contracts` must use identical task inputs,
model configuration, runtime, tools, limits, and verifier; only agent identity and code-contracts
skill exposure may differ.

@cc [author:spolu,label:security] benchmark-information-isolation
Agent-visible inputs must never include DeepSWE solution artifacts, verifier implementation,
held-out tests, or information derived from them.

@cc [author:spolu,label:reproducibility] scored-run-provenance
Each scored run must record immutable identifiers or digests for its dataset, task manifest,
harness, agent, tools, skill prompt, model, reasoning configuration, and resolved run configuration.

@cc [author:spolu,label:security] secret-non-persistence
Credentials and secret values must enter through the runtime environment and never be written to
images, committed configuration, prompts, trajectories, logs, or result artifacts.

@cc [author:spolu,label:evaluation] outcome-integrity
Raw trial artifacts must remain unmodified, and retries or exclusions must follow predeclared rules
that apply identically to both arms.
